      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This issue has resurfaced for several days now.  Tried to force-quit only to report back \"empty process\".  Can't restart until it finally quits 3 to 4 minutes later.  Tried validating and the problem still exists.  It does not matter whether in VR or on desktop.  Log did not report any abnormal activity on exit.\n\nUPDATE: last time this occurred probably a legacy asset using one core (of a multi-core processor) and it suddenly steals a lot of resources until it's finally able to receive the quit message to stop.  Tested some worlds and it happens to be one or possibly more than one asset doing this.  Not sure which one, haven't dug any further.  No idea why unless it got blocked from accessing?  IDK.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
